>> title: Buri Daikon
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: japanese, yellowtail, daikon, simmered, fish, winter
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: ぶり大根, buri daikon, buri daikon, ブリ大根, 鰤大根, yellowtail and daikon, simmered yellowtail with radish
>> pairs-with: gohan, sumashi-jiru
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — past about half an hour in the pot the collar goes dry and stringy, and reducing the glaze puts no fat back

>> step: A 煮魚: the liquid is water and not dashi — water 5 : soy 1 : mirin 1 : sake 1.
A 煮魚, so the liquid is water and not dashi — water 5 : soy 1 : mirin 1 : sake 1.

>> step: parboil 20 min in rice water
Parboil @daikon{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; peeled, in 1-inch rounds with the corners pared off) in @rice-washing water{2%qt}(2 L; the cloudy water off rinsing rice, or 2 qt water with 1 Tbs raw rice) ~parboil{20%min}, until a skewer meets slight resistance at the centre, then rinse the pieces.

>> step: scald and rinse
Pour @boiling water{4%cups}(950 mL; straight off the kettle) over @yellowtail collar{1 1/4%lb}(570 g; in pieces, or 4 steaks) in a #colander{} until the surfaces turn white, then rinse each piece and pick off the loosened scales and blood.

>> step: simmer 25 min under a drop lid
Simmer @&(2)parboiled daikon{} and @&(~1)scalded buri{} in @water{1 1/4%cups}(300 mL) with @soy sauce{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @mirin{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @sake{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @sugar{2%Tbs} and @ginger{1%piece}(2 in, sliced thin) in a #wide pot{} under a drop lid ~simmer{25%min}, in one layer and never at more than a lazy bubble.

>> step: spoon over 10 min, uncovered
Lift the drop lid off @&(~1)pot{} and ~reduce{10%min}, spooning the liquid over the fish every minute or so, until it has darkened and thickened enough to coat the daikon.
